                    "slice's document: the one it was saved from, the doc naming its",
                    "type, or a stub built from the mount fact's startSource — every",
                    "mounted slice opens as the code that is actually executing.",
                    "The workspace boots empty — no seed document, nothing open — so",
                    "open one before editing: SliceCreateRequested seeds slice-N (the",
                    "first is slice-1) and an edit with nothing open lands nowhere;",
                    "SliceDuplicateRequested",
                    "copies under a fresh type; SliceDeleteRequested deletes the",
                    "document and unmounts the instance the foundry saved. The last",
                    "document is immortal, and compiled-in slices are not the",
                    "foundry's to kill. Every BufferChanged and BufferRestored carries",
                    "fileIds — the roster of documents that exist — so a listener",
                    "learns a deletion or a scrub-restored workspace from the outcome",
                    "fact, never from the intent; the digest says `docs: +id -id`",
